    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Electrical Conductivity Formula\n\n**σ = J / E**\n\nWhere:\n- σ = electrical conductivity (1/Ω m, S/m, mho/m)\n- J = current density (amps/m²)\n- E = electric field strength (volts/m)\n\n## Electrical Resistivity Formula\n\n**ρ = 1 / σ**\n\nWhere:\n- ρ = electrical resistivity (ohm m)\n- σ = electrical conductivity (S/m)\n\n## Resistance of a Conductor\n\n**R = ρ l / A**\n\nWhere:\n- R = resistance (ohms, Ω)\n- l = length of conductor (m)\n- A = cross sectional area of conductor (m²)\n\n## Unit Conversions\n\n- 1 S/m = 10⁴ μS/cm = mho/m\n- 1 S/cm = 10⁻² S/m\n- 1 1/Ω m = S/m = 3.28 1/Ω ft = 3.28 S/ft\n- 1 grains/gal = 17.1 ppm CaCO₃"
